  "findingsAndConclusions": [
    "One profile binds the accepted fresh executor R2 config, all five executable roles, source pins and exact source-review decision/filename-role aliases. Fresh result, parent and lane paths match its config.",
    "All nine helper functions remain exact original AST/source. Whole forward/inverse pairs for filler and profiles restore the authenticated accepted base bytes. Necessary changes only rebind current AM, one diagnostic proof profile, four authenticated external diagnostic prerequisites and associated hashes.",
    "External true root specification is required. Four diagnostic role schemas/hashes/bytes are authenticated before immutable context emission; deeper producer semantics are enforced by accepted executor before private traversal. Context contains only existing prerequisite roles, null future source/dependency/protection proofs and a grant that binds the context excluding itself.",
    "Owned PID/PGID/SID is durably recorded before context/grant and same-PID direct exec. Collision checks make the fixed parent emissions once-only; the original lane lock is authenticated and rebound immediately before exec.",
    "Pinned real tools/physical/link identities, Node22, isolated no-bytecode Python, exact working directory and inherited HOME remain enforced. Preparation60 is canceled immediately before LAUNCH; original launch330/recorder320/runner300 begins there. No combined or outer runtime watchdog is claimed."
  ],
